1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:06,570
When your phone rings, you don't control the phone. The phone controls you.

2
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:09,540
Master, one minute, a message came!

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,260
Diyor, listen.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,050
2006, America.

5
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:19,090
An engineer invented infinite scrolling:

6
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:22,400
the page never ends, you just keep scrolling down.

7
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,150
When a page ends, you stop.

8
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,050
When it doesn't, you don't.

9
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:33,840
Later he openly said he regretted his invention.

10
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:37,010
Do apps keep us hooked on purpose?!

11
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:42,810
According to one study, the average user gets close to forty-six notifications a day.

12
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:47,060
Apps make money from your attention:

13
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:51,290
the longer you look, the more ads they show.

14
00:00:51,790 --> 00:00:52,950
Three rules.

15
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:55,500
Turn off useless notifications.

16
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,360
Turn on silent mode at night.

17
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,910
Before opening an app, ask:

18
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,070
why am I opening it?

19
00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:03,940
Phone silent, me calm!

20
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:10,930
They don't sell you the app, they sell you the fear of “missing out”.

21
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:11,970
Every time, ask:

22
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:14,050
who profits from this?

23
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:20,250
If you don't know which notification to turn off, write the app's name to our bot:

24
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:21,270
@sahiychishopbot.

25
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:23,110
It teaches you step by step.

